---
name: video_audio_transcription_check
description: "Check a finished video mix by transcription so only the intended voice is heard, whenever a video carries voiceover over music or a reused soundtrack. Improved version with frame and loudness checks."
---

# Video Audio Transcription Check

## Transcribe the finished mix

- Transcribe the final mixed audio from start to finish and list every spoken phrase in order.

- Compare every transcribed phrase with the intended script and flag any phrase that is not in that script.

- Reject the mix when an unscripted phrase appears even when that phrase is quiet or buried under music.

- Deliver a mix only after its transcription matches the intended script exactly.

## Transcribe the music bed alone

- Transcribe the music track on its own before mixing it under any voice.

- Reject a reused soundtrack when its own transcription contains any words because lowering its volume does not remove a hidden voice.

- Replace a rejected bed with a purely instrumental track and transcribe that replacement on its own before use.

- Treat a bed that transcribes to zero words as the only bed that is safe to mix under a voice.

## Check loudness and frames with the audio

- Measure the final mix loudness and peaks and keep a short form video near minus 14 LUFS with true peaks at or below minus 3 dB unless the platform asks otherwise.

- Extract frames from every scene and check them in the same pass as the transcription.

- Reject the delivery when a frame shows truncated text, a sticker covering a key word or an empty static scene, even when the audio passes.

## Fix and recheck before delivery

- Remove the source of any unscripted voice instead of masking it with volume changes or ducking.

- Rebuild the mix after the fix and transcribe the new mix again from start to finish.

- Report the transcription result in plain words with the count of intended phrases found and confirmation that no unscripted phrase remains.

## Available connectors

- Use `muse.connector_search` to find other connectors and `muse.skill_search` to find related skills.

- If nothing here fits, look on the web for a maintained API or MCP server and set it up with Custom Connectors and MCPs, or build a custom connector.

## Alternatives for better results

- Ask for separate voice and music stems when reusing a format soundtrack so voice and music can be checked apart.

- Use a newly composed instrumental bed when the source of a reused track cannot be verified.

- Keep the intended script to one voice in one language so the transcription comparison stays exact.
